# GitHub Actions CI/CD Configuration

## Workflow Trigger Rules

• Trigger on pull requests to main/dev
• Run on all branch pushes
• Support manual workflow dispatch
• Use workflow_run for dependencies
• Enable branch-specific CI patterns

```yaml
on:
  pull_request:
    branches: [main, dev]
  push:
    branches: ["**"]
  workflow_dispatch:
```

## Environment Configuration

• Pin Flutter version to 3.35.4
• Use Java 17 for Android builds
• Configure pub cache workspace location
• Set consistent timeout limits
• Define global environment variables

```yaml
env:
  JAVA_VERSION: "17"
  FLUTTER_VERSION: "3.35.4"
  PUB_CACHE: ${{ github.workspace }}/.pub-cache
```

## Caching Strategy Rules

• Cache Flutter SDK with version key
• Cache pub dependencies with hash key
• Cache Dart analysis results
• Use restore-keys for fallback
• Pre-warm caches in prepare job

```yaml
- name: Cache Flutter SDK
  uses: actions/cache@v4
  with:
    path: |
      /opt/hostedtoolcache/flutter
      ~/.flutter
    key: flutter-${{ env.FLUTTER_VERSION }}-${{ runner.os }}
```

## Job Dependency Management

• Use prepare job for cache warming
• Define clear job dependencies with needs
• Run lint and test in parallel
• Require integration tests before builds
• Use outputs for cache key sharing

```yaml
jobs:
  prepare:
    outputs:
      flutter-cache-key: ${{ steps.cache-keys.outputs.flutter-key }}
  lint:
    needs: prepare
  test:
    needs: [prepare]
```

## Quality Assurance Rules

• Run dart format with exit-if-changed
• Execute flutter analyze with fatal warnings
• Check for unused dependencies
• Audit for security vulnerabilities
• Validate project structure requirements

```yaml
- name: Verify formatting
  run: dart format --output=none --set-exit-if-changed .
- name: Analyze project source
  run: flutter analyze --fatal-infos --fatal-warnings
```

## Testing Configuration

• Run tests with coverage enabled
• Use random test ordering
• Upload coverage artifacts
• Check coverage thresholds
• Cache test results for efficiency

```yaml
- name: Run tests
  run: flutter test --coverage --test-randomize-ordering-seed random
```

## Security Scanning Rules

• Check for hardcoded API keys
• Scan for password literals
• Detect secret value patterns
• Block debug prints in production
• Validate token assignment patterns

```yaml
if grep -rE "(sk_|pk_|bearer\s+)[a-zA-Z0-9]{20,}" lib/ --include="*.dart"; then
  echo "Potential API key pattern found"
  exit 1
fi
```

## Integration Testing Setup

• Enable KVM for Android emulator
• Cache Android Virtual Device images
• Use API level 30 x86_64
• Configure emulator options properly
• Run integration tests on emulator

```yaml
- name: Enable KVM group perms
  run: |
    echo 'KERNEL=="kvm", GROUP="kvm", MODE="0666"' | sudo tee /etc/udev/rules.d/99-kvm4all.rules
```

## Build Configuration Rules

• Use Temurin Java distribution
• Build debug APK with run number
• Define minimum SDK version
• Upload build artifacts
• Verify APK size limits

```yaml
- name: Build Android APK
  run: flutter build apk --debug --build-number=${{ github.run_number }} --dart-define=MIN_SDK_VERSION=24
```

## Documentation Validation

• Require README.md file presence
• Check for LICENSE file
• Validate SECURITY.md exists
• Ensure PRIVACY.md is present
• Fail on missing documentation

```yaml
required_files=("README.md" "LICENSE" "SECURITY.md" "PRIVACY.md")
for file in "${required_files[@]}"; do
  if [ ! -f "$file" ]; then
    exit 1
  fi
done
```

## Artifact Management

• Upload coverage reports
• Store APK artifacts temporarily
• Set 7-day retention period
• Name artifacts descriptively
• Use versioned upload actions

```yaml
- name: Upload APK artifact
  uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
  with:
    name: android-apk-debug
    retention-days: 7
```

## Timeout and Performance

• Set 15-minute prepare timeout
• Limit lint jobs to 10 minutes
• Allow 30 minutes for builds
• Use 15-minute test timeouts
• Optimize with parallel execution